# .trivyignore — Trivy vulnerability/secret suppressions for privacy-toolkit
# Format: <CVE-ID or finding-id> [optional expiry: until=YYYY-MM-DD] [optional comment]
# See: https://aquasecurity.github.io/trivy/latest/docs/configuration/filtering/#trivyignore

# ── Test / dev-only dependencies ──────────────────────────────────────────────
# pytest, ruff, and similar tools are never in the production image;
# suppress findings from these when running `trivy fs` on the whole repo.

# ── Known accepted risks (document rationale + expiry for each) ───────────────
# Example:
# CVE-YYYY-XXXXX  until=2026-12-31  # low-impact, no fix available, mitigated by network isolation

# ── Helm misconfig false positives ────────────────────────────────────────────

# KSV-0109: ConfigMap 'anonymizer-config' — triggered by the comment
# "# Dual-pass" in a YAML config file. Not a secret value.
KSV-0109

# KSV-01010: ConfigMap 'fhir-server-config' — triggered by Spring Boot
# in-memory H2 datasource keys "username: sa" / "password: ''".
# H2 is the in-process dev/test DB; no real credentials are stored here.
KSV-01010

# KSV-0125: HAPI FHIR uses hapiproject/hapi (Docker Hub) — a known trusted
# registry for the open-source HAPI FHIR server project. Not a supply-chain risk.
KSV-0125

# KSV-0012: postgres containers use gosu to drop privileges at runtime;
# runAsNonRoot cannot be set because the entrypoint starts as root (UID 0)
# and chowns the data directory before exec'ing as the postgres user (UID 70/999).
# This is the documented upstream postgres image behavior.
KSV-0012

# KSV-0014: postgres requires a writable filesystem (data, run, tmp directories).
# readOnlyRootFilesystem cannot be enabled without complex init-container setups
# that are out of scope for this embedded database deployment.
KSV-0014

# KSV-0118: postgres pod uses default securityContext intentionally —
# see comments for KSV-0012/0014 above. Pod-level seccompProfile is added.
KSV-0118

# ── Output / generated files ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
output/
.venv/
.venv-slides/
node_modules/
# cache is written to /tmp/trivy-cache (no local cache dir)

# ── Local dev RSA key (gitignored; never committed) ───────────────────────────
# Generated by: openssl genrsa -out services/anonymizer/keys/id_rsa 4096
# Suppressed via skip-files in trivy.yaml (path-based secret suppression
# in .trivyignore is not supported in Trivy v0.71).
